' What the scene's loading spinner is waiting on. Each kind has its own rules for what the
' viewer is told and what Back does: see docs/architecture/navigation.md ("What kind of wait
' a spinner is") and source/utils/loadingStages.bs.
enum LoadingKind
  ' Not yet assigned a kind: the spinner and the caller's text, nothing else. Every
  ' startLoadingSpinner() call is this until its call site moves to an intent-named start.
  PLAIN = "plain"
  ' A screen waiting on the server for the data it shows (screenWaits.begin), or the scene's
  ' own cast resolve. Back leaves; after 8 s the viewer is told it is still loading, and after
  ' 30 s that the wait is the server's.
  CONTENT = "content"
  ' Playback starting, from the press to the player holding a stream (appWaits.begin through
  ' QueueManager.beginPlaybackStart), or a photo or slideshow from the press to its first photo
  ' showing. An app wait: it outlives the screen that started it.
  ' Same stages as CONTENT, under the channel label on a channel switch. Back cancels it and
  ' shows the screen it was pressed on again; other keys wait for it (AppWaitHost).
  PLAYBACK_START = "playbackStart"
  ' A sign-in step the viewer pressed: a server connect, a user pick, a password or Quick Connect
  ' sign-in, a server switch. An app wait opened by the press, which the next screen mounting
  ' ends. It hides the screen it was pressed on and holds the keys; Back cancels it and shows
  ' that screen again, until the step commits (appWaits.commit) and only local work is left
  ' (ADR 0053). No stage text.
  SESSION = "session"
  ' An action the viewer pressed that stays on its screen, such as a details Refresh. An app wait
  ' opened by the press, which its answer ends. It hides the screen it was pressed on and holds
  ' the keys; Back cancels it, shows that screen again, and the late answer is dropped
  ' (ADR 0053). No stage text.
  ACTION = "action"
  ' An action the viewer pressed whose answer opens over the screen it was pressed on (a dialog),
  ' such as the SyncPlay menu's group list. An app wait like ACTION: it holds the keys and Back
  ' cancels it. The screen stays in view, since nothing on it changes. No stage text.
  OVERLAY = "overlay"
  ' The player waiting on its own stream, such as an audio seek that loads a new one. A screen
  ' wait on the player (screenWaits.begin): the player stays on show and takes only Back, which
  ' leaves it. No stage text: the wait is the player's, not a server answer to report.
  BUFFERING = "buffering"
end enum
